{"event_id":"EVT-000052","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-28T07:13:35.749Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260828T040224480510Z","run_id":"RUN-TRF-009-20260828T071147244032Z","requirement_id":"TRF-009","event_type":"validator_feedback_possible_reversal","iteration":2,"prior_feedback_history":["The applicable branch overconstrains the requirement by making engineOutputComplianceMethod mandatory even when the assessment date is before the 1 January deadline. The obligation is due only when the assessment date has reached or passed the deadline; before that date, a missing method must not fail the shape. Conditionalize the permitted-method requirement and deadline check so that assessmentDate <= 1 January of delivery year plus 20 is allowed without the method, while assessmentDate >= that deadline requires one of the two permitted methods. Preserve the existing ship ownership, IA/IA Super applicability, and construction-date boundary."],"current_feedback":"Preserve the prior conditional deadline instruction, but repair two accidental-pass paths. First, the applicability/date constraint requires a constructionStageDate triple before it can report missing dates; an applicable IA/IA Super ship with no constructionStageDate therefore passes silently. Add an explicit applicable-ship violation for missing constructionStageDate, while requiring assessmentDate and deliveryDate only after the construction date is present and before 1 September 2003. Second, gate the permitted/invalid engineOutputComplianceMethod check itself on assessmentDate being on or after 1 January of delivery year plus 20. Before that deadline, a missing method\u2014and any method-status check\u2014must not fail; on or after it, require one of the two permitted controlled values and reject invalid values.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
